## A Remote Presenter, Not a Full Virtual Event

A remote presentation is narrower than a full virtual or hybrid event: it is usually one remote speaker or participant joining an otherwise in-person room, not an entire conference run online. If your event is fully virtual or has a large remote audience alongside an in-person one, see our [audio visual rental for virtual events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-virtual-events/) guide instead.

For a single remote presenter or a call-in Q&A, our [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) covers a 5000-lumen laser projector and screen for the call, PA sound so the room hears it, and a wireless handheld microphone so the room's questions reach the remote side. For a smaller boardroom meeting, the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) covers the same idea with a gooseneck microphone and a 3000 lumen projector and screen, up to 40 guests.

<InlineCTA />

## What We Provide vs. What You Bring

**We provide**: PA sound and a microphone so the room can hear and be heard, a projector and screen sized to the room, and the adapters to connect your own laptop to both.

**You bring**: your own laptop or device, your video conferencing software, and your internet connection. We do not provide cameras, webcams or streaming equipment.

## Connecting Your Own Laptop

Our [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) includes HDMI and USB-C adapters plus audio interfaces to connect your own laptop, tablet or media player to our sound and screen setup. Stepping up to a larger conference room? The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) swaps in a bigger 60 inch LED display and includes a dedicated technician for up to six hours, and can carry the same laptop adapters over on request; just mention it when you book.

