## FAQs

### What equipment do I need for a remote presentation?

Room sound so people can hear the call, a screen so they can see it, and a way to connect your laptop to both. Our [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) covers all three with HDMI and USB-C adapters included. See [A Remote Presenter, Not a Full Virtual Event](#a-remote-presenter-not-a-full-virtual-event) above.

### What is the difference between a remote presentation and a virtual event?

A remote presentation is usually one remote speaker or participant joining an otherwise in-person room. A virtual event covers a full session or conference run mostly or entirely online. Either way, we supply the same thing: the room's sound, screen and laptop connectivity. See our [audio visual rental for virtual events](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-virtual-events/) guide for the larger case.

### Can a remote presenter join an in-person meeting or event?

Yes. Connect your own laptop or video call to our screen and sound system through the adapters included on the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/), and the room can see and hear the remote presenter without any extra equipment.

### Do you provide cameras or webcams for remote presentations?

No. We provide the room's sound and screen, not cameras, webcams or streaming equipment. You run the call from your own laptop and software.

### Can I use my own laptop with your setup?

Yes, the [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) comes with HDMI and USB-C adapters, plus audio interfaces, so you can plug in a laptop, tablet or media player directly.

### What size package do I need for a small remote-participant meeting?

For a boardroom-scale meeting, the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) covers up to 40 guests with a gooseneck microphone and a projector and screen. For a larger conference room, the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) covers up to 120 guests with a 60 inch LED display and a technician included.

### Do you provide internet or wifi for the call?

No. Internet and wifi are not included in any of our packages, so confirm connectivity with your venue ahead of the event.

### Is a technician included for a remote presentation setup?

Not on every package. The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) includes a technician on site for up to six hours; on the Basic MICE Pack a technician is available as an add on. Ask when you book.

### How much does audio visual rental cost for a remote presentation?

Pricing depends on the package: our full catalog, from the Basic MICE Pack up to the MICE Pack for a larger conference room, is listed with exact euro pricing on our [packages page](/packages/). All rates are ex VAT, with 21 percent Spanish VAT added at checkout, and every price includes delivery, setup and teardown.
